course: dictionary
lesson: 12652
title: Ignoring on purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To disregard something is to pay it no attention, so you ignore it on purpose. «Sam disregarded the sign and walked on the closed path.» Sam saw the sign and chose not to follow it. The sentence tells you what he did, and the word disregarded tells you he did it on purpose.
explain: Disregard can also be a noun, meaning a lack of care. «The driver's disregard for safety worried everyone.» Here disregard is the thing the driver showed. It means he did not care enough about safety, so he was careless.
explain: Look at the words around disregard to check its meaning. Words like «please» and «complete» are clues. «Please disregard my last message» means please ignore it, and «complete disregard for the rules» means not caring about the rules at all.
fact: Disregard means to pay no attention to something, or to ignore it on purpose.
fact: As a noun, disregard means a lack of care or attention, especially for rules, safety or other people's feelings.
fact: In maths, «disregard the units» tells you to leave the units out.
fact: Phrases to learn: disregard the rules, complete disregard for, please disregard.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping in ignore: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Sam disregarded the sign and walked on the closed path.» What does disregarded mean? | Followed it carefully | Read it aloud | *Paid no attention to | Copied it down
exercise: «Disregard the units when you add the numbers.» What should you do with the units? | *Leave them out | Turn them into a fraction | Add them as well | Write them twice
exercise: «The driver's disregard for safety worried everyone.» What does disregard mean here? | Careful attention | Strong dislike | Quick thinking | *Lack of care
test: «Please disregard my last message, I sent it by mistake.» What does please disregard mean? | *Ignore it | Send it again | Save it | Read it twice
test: «Ben showed complete disregard for the rules.» What does this tell you about Ben? | *He did not care about the rules | He knew all the rules by heart | He was happy to follow them | He wrote the rules
exam: Which word means paying no attention to something on purpose? | Attention | Respect | *Disregard | Remember
